        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "normalization. The snapshots cover the 50–225 MHz band with uniform channel spacing  $ \\Delta\\nu \\approx 0.3418 $ MHz and time resolution  $ \\Delta t = 1.0 $ s. For the HERA analysis, we define the science core as 140–160 MHz, the science band as 130–170 MHz, and the outside band as the remaining channels. The synthetic channel spacing ( $ \\Delta\\nu = 0.05 $ MHz) is finer than the HERA spacing ( $ \\approx 0.34 $ MHz) in order to resolve narrowband RFI more clearly; this affects the apparent rank of narrowband structure but not the underlying non-identifiability mechanism, which is driven by subspace overlap.",
            "block_bbox": [
